-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Downloaded onto the user's machine at first launch
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Python environment that serves safetensors models is built on the user's
machine from the lockfiles in vendor/python. None of it is redistributed by
this project, so none of it carries an obligation here. It is listed because
someone auditing what a LocalNEXUS install contains will find it on disk.

The set is pinned by vendor/python/requirements-cu132.txt and
requirements-cpu.txt. The packages it is built around:

  transformers      Apache License 2.0    https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
  torch             BSD 3-Clause          https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch
  accelerate        Apache License 2.0    https://github.com/huggingface/accelerate
  requests          Apache License 2.0    https://github.com/psf/requests
  fastapi           MIT License           https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi
  uvicorn           BSD 3-Clause          https://github.com/encode/uvicorn

Everything else in those lockfiles arrives as a dependency of one of the above
and carries its own license, readable in the installed environment under
%LOCALAPPDATA%\LocalNEXUS\runtime\python.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compatibility
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every license above is compatible with the Apache License 2.0 this project is
released under. MIT and BSD 3-Clause are permissive and impose only attribution,
which this file provides. The SIL Open Font License restricts selling the font
on its own and requires its license text to travel with the font, neither of
which this project does or omits. Nothing here is copyleft, so no dependency
reaches back and constrains how LocalNEXUS itself may be licensed.
